      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "The community appears to be conducting a mass immunization campaign aimed at wiping out an endemic pathogen.",
          "grammar": "appear to be＋現在分詞 / aimed at＋動名詞 / wipe out",
          "ja": "この地域では、地域に常在する病原体を根絶することを目的とした大規模予防接種が行われているようです。",
          "type": "gist",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "To wipe out an endemic pathogen means to eliminate an infectious agent that has persistently circulated within a particular population or region.",
          "grammar": "to不定詞主語 / 関係代名詞that / 現在完了形",
          "ja": "「wipe out an endemic pathogen」とは、特定の集団や地域内で継続的に流行してきた病原体を根絶することを意味します。",
          "type": "gist",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Healthcare workers are systematically vaccinating local residents in an effort to interrupt chains of transmission.",
          "grammar": "現在進行形 / in an effort to",
          "ja": "医療従事者たちは感染の連鎖を断つため、地域住民に体系的に予防接種を行っています。",
          "type": "detail",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "The presence of a vaccine cooler suggests that maintaining an appropriate cold chain is an important part of the campaign.",
          "grammar": "suggest that / 動名詞主語",
          "ja": "ワクチン用保冷ボックスがあることから、適切なコールドチェーンの維持がこの活動の重要な要素であることがうかがえます。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "If a sufficiently large proportion of the population becomes immune, opportunities for the pathogen to spread may decline dramatically.",
          "grammar": "If / become＋形容詞 / may",
          "ja": "人口の十分に大きな割合が免疫を獲得すれば、病原体が広がる機会は大幅に減少する可能性があります。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Widespread immunization can reduce prevalence and, in favorable circumstances, eventually eliminate local transmission altogether.",
          "grammar": "動名詞主語 / can / 並列動詞",
          "ja": "広範な予防接種は疾病の蔓延度を低下させ、条件が整えば最終的に地域内感染そのものをなくすことも可能です。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Eradicating an endemic pathogen generally requires sustained coverage rather than a single round of vaccination.",
          "grammar": "動名詞主語 / require / rather than",
          "ja": "地域に常在する病原体を根絶するには、一般に一度だけの予防接種ではなく、継続的に高い接種率を維持する必要があります。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "The orderly registration process indicates that the initiative is being coordinated across the wider community.",
          "grammar": "indicate that / 現在進行形の受動態",
          "ja": "整然とした受付・記録作業から、この取り組みが地域全体で組織的に実施されていることが分かります。",
          "type": "detail",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Overall, the scene provides useful practice in describing efforts to wipe out an endemic pathogen through vaccination, immunization, transmission control, disease eradication, and coordinated public-health intervention.",
          "grammar": "to不定詞 / through＋名詞 / 列挙",
          "ja": "全体として、この場面は予防接種、免疫付与、感染制御、疾病根絶、組織的な公衆衛生介入によって地域固有の病原体を根絶する取り組みを描写する練習に適しています。",
          "type": "gist",
